{"id": "ee237ecf-adde-4541-8cea-98eb92434ca9", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I can't confirm the exact control number in documentation, so I'll answer from memory—CIS EKS benchmark control 4.1.7 "Avoid use of system:masters group" appears across different benchmark versions, though I'm uncertain which exact version aligns with this numbering.

Given the evidence—alice mapped to system:masters in aws-auth, which bypasses RBAC entirely and remains effective since authenticationMode is API_AND_CONFIG_MAP—this is a FAIL. The node role mapping looks fine (system:nodes, not masters). My remediation: remove alice from aws-auth, replace with an access entry using AmazonEKSClusterAdminPolicy or a scoped RBAC group, and ideally migrate toward API-only authentication mode, keeping in mind access entries and cluster-creator admin aren't part of what's being evaluated here.

